 "lesson": {
  "slides": [
   {
    "id": "L1",
    "type": "expr",
    "text": "$$f(x) = x^2 - 3x$$\nA function is a rule with blanks in it. Whatever you put inside $f( )$ goes into **every** blank.\nPut 5 in and watch.",
    "answer": "5",
    "vars": [],
    "label": "Input:",
    "show": "$5$",
    "hint": "Type 5.",
    "explain": "$f(5) = (5)^2 - 3(5) = 10$. One input, and it lands in every blank.",
    "template": "f([]) = ([])^2 - 3([])"
   },
   {
    "id": "L2",
    "type": "num",
    "text": "A negative input needs its parentheses.$$f(-2) = (-2)^2 - 3(-2)$$\nWhat number is that?",
    "answer": 10,
    "label": "$f(-2)$ =",
    "hint": "$(-2)^2 = 4$ and $-3(-2) = +6$.",
    "explain": "$4 + 6 = 10$. Without the parentheses, $-2^2$ would have been $-4$."
   },
   {
    "id": "L3",
    "type": "expr",
    "text": "$$f(x) = x^2 - 3x$$\nThe input does not have to be a number. Put $x + h$ into the blanks.",
    "answer": "x + h",
    "vars": [
     "x",
     "h"
    ],
    "label": "Input:",
    "show": "$x + h$",
    "hint": "Type x + h. The rule does not change, only what sits in the blanks.",
    "explain": "$f(x + h) = (x + h)^2 - 3(x + h)$. Nothing else about the rule changed.",
    "template": "f([]) = ([])^2 - 3([])"
   },
   {
    "id": "L4",
    "type": "mc",
    "text": "To finish, you have to multiply out $(x + h)^2$. Which is it?",
